      </modifiers>
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="898e-c209-980c-cd9f" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
      </constraints>
      <rules>
        <rule id="f213-36e5-a063-009c" name="Ætheric Blessing: Formless Distortion" hidden="false">
          <description>At the start of each of the controlling player's turns, before any units are moved, select one of the following mutations for each unit with this Ætheric Blessing until the start of the controlling player's next turn. Razor-Limbs: models in the unit gain +1 Attack in the Assault phase. Chitinous Carapace: models in the unit gain +1 Toughness (to a maximum of T 8). Distorted Silhouette: models in the unit gain the Shrouded (5+) special rule.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink id="7f53-7b2f-3b7d-12d9" name="Formless Distortion" hidden="false" targetId="9556-82c1-c70a-126e" primary="false"/>
      </categoryLinks>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
  </sharedSelectionEntries>
  <catalogueLinks>
    <catalogueLink type="catalogue" name="Daemon Library" id="6a4d-7b3c-1cc1-591e" targetId="31bf-eb23-33a-3d65"/>
    <catalogueLink type="catalogue" name="LI - Assassins and Agents" id="8e51-2e3c-9a19-fa1" targetId="4c88-1a81-7e53-0a67"/>
  </catalogueLinks>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Immaterial Blades (X)" hidden="false" id="8d0-4d35-7d40-bc09" publicationId="8775-88f5-cfdd-24f6" page="22">
      <description>When rolling To Wound for a model that has the Immaterial Blades (X) special rule, or is attacking with a weapon that has the Immaterial Blades (X) special rule, for each To Wound roll or Armour Penetration roll of 6 or higher, the controlling player resolves these Wounds or any Penetrating Hits at the AP value listed in brackets, instead of the weapon’s normal AP value.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Unbound" hidden="false" id="40ce-bba7-f433-6089" publicationId="8775-88f5-cfdd-24f6" page="22">
      <description>Some Daemons, such as Ka’bandha or Samus, have multiple profiles, presenting the different manners in which they manifest. A model with this rule cannot be included in the same army as its Bound version – an army that includes Samus Unbound cannot also include Samus Bound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Herald of Unreality" hidden="false" id="76ba-1913-c091-2860" publicationId="8775-88f5-cfdd-24f6" page="22">
      <description>An army that includes a model with this rule may select up to two units from the same Detachment that have the Daemon Unit Type to be deployed in Reserve at the beginning of the battle. If an army includes more than one model with this rule, they may select one additional unit that has the Daemon Unit Type to place in Reserve for each model in the army with this rule beyond the first. The chosen units may only enter play by means of a Warp Rift – no Reserves rolls are made for these units.

For example, an army with three models with the Herald of Unreality special rule would be able to select up to four non-Lords of War choices with the Daemon Unit Type to be deployed in Reserve. Instead of making a Shooting Attack, the controlling player of a model with this special rule may place a Blast (3&quot;) Marker in base contact with that model and not over any other models to represent the Warp Rift.

The model’s controlling player may then choose to move one of the Daemon units that were placed into Reserves using this special rule onto the battlefield. That unit moves onto the battlefield from any point along the edge of the Blast marker placed to represent the Warp Rift as if it was entering play from Reserves, treating the Warp Rift marker as though it was the controlling player’s battlefield edge (note that it is not treated as the controlling player’s battlefield edge for any other purposes).

Once all models in the selected units have moved onto the battlefield, the Warp Rift marker is removed from play. The Daemon unit brought into play by use of this power may act as normal in the Shooting phase in which it arrives and may declare a Charge in the Assault phase of the turn in which it enters play.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Daemons of the Ruinstorm" id="96c8-8244-551e-fb18" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit with this special rule belongs to the Daemons of the Ruinstorm, is part of the Traitor Alliance and has the Traitor special rule. It may only be taken in a Detachment of the Daemons of the Ruinstorm.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Daemonic (X)" id="69eb-cbfa-a5f6-db1d" hidden="false">
      <description>A model with this special rule has an Invulnerable Save of X.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Harbinger of Execution" id="8a6c-c8ab-3f4a-295e" hidden="false">
      <description>A model with this special rule occupies an HQ Force Organisation slot, may not be selected as the army's Warlord, and does not count toward the minimum number of Compulsory HQ choices required in a Detachment. A Detachment may only include a Daemonic Assassin whose Ætheric Dominion matches the Detachment's chosen Dominion (or any single Daemonic Assassin if the Detachment is aligned to Formless Distortion).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hunter of Champions" id="fa89-c2d9-39fd-b963" hidden="false">
      <description>When resolving close combat attacks or Shooting Attacks against a unit containing at least one model with the Character or Unique Unit Sub-type, a model with this special rule re-rolls all failed To Wound rolls and gains +1 to its Combat Resolution score if it slays an enemy Character in a Challenge.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Soul Blaze" id="cbb5-aa7c-8556-d5ee" hidden="false">
      <description>At the end of each turn, roll a D6 for each enemy unit that suffered one or more unsaved wounds from a weapon with Soul Blaze that turn: on a 4+, the unit suffers D3 Strength 4, AP 5 hits with the Ignores Cover special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Melta" id="6ba6-9721-0a57-760f" hidden="false">
      <description>A weapon with this special rule rolls an additional D6 for Armour Penetration when the target is within half its maximum range.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Paired Weapon" id="7ae8-88d1-c8e9-c5d1" hidden="false">
      <description>A model armed with this weapon gains +1 Attack, as if it were armed with two close combat weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="2413-dc1e-778d-5e66" hidden="false">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="05a4-0149-d82e-3f9f" name="Master of the Ruinstorm" hidden="false">
      <description>A Ruinstorm Daemon Sovereign or Ruinstorm Daemon Harbinger is treated as having the Master of the Legion special rule in every way: it may be the army's Warlord, it lets its Detachment select a Rite of War, and it counts toward the number of models with Master of the Legion an army may include.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <selectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="false" name="Ætheric Dominion (Whole Army)" hidden="false" id="f6d5-4f8d-7bcc-1405">
      <profiles>
        <profile id="41c9-54f9-01d3-8569" name="Advanced Reaction: Empyric Surge (Movement Phase)" hidden="false" typeId="90b9-7fab-87db-aed3" typeName="Reactions">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="c627-4637-8de5-65fb">Trigger: This Advanced Reaction may be declared in the Movement phase, immediately after an enemy unit ends a move within 12" of, and within line of sight of, a friendly unit composed entirely of models with the Daemon Unit Type.
Effect: Every model in the reacting unit may immediately make a move of up to D6 + its Initiative Characteristic in inches directly toward the triggering enemy unit. This move ignores Difficult Terrain, and if it brings any model in the reacting unit within 1" of an enemy model from that unit, move the reacting models into base contact; the reacting unit is locked in combat and counts as having made a successful Charge for the ensuing Assault phase. A unit with the Putrid Corruption Dominion may still declare this Advanced Reaction, but rolls D3 instead of D6 for its movement distance.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink targetId="5d31-e5d-67bd-1083" id="1b05-8967-710b-6c83" primary="true" name="Ætheric Dominion (Whole Army)"/>
      </categoryLinks>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink import="true" name="The Ætheric Dominion (X)" hidden="false" type="selectionEntryGroup" id="9508-a542-880a-8a31" targetId="002f-0e40-9d49-2a22"/>
      </entryLinks>
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="267a-1750-8ebf-a325"/>
        <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="7c7f-7835-4b73-7a69"/>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" shared="true" id="967c-ba3e-e226-faa0"/>
