                <modifier type="set" field="6f5a-c37f-dfb3-93b8" value="0">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="a24f-12d8-36c1-f477" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="6f5a-c37f-dfb3-93b8" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule id="12f7-b501-c789-e5f4" name="Prerequisites" hidden="false">
                  <description>• A Detachment using this Rite of War must include a Ruinstorm Daemon Sovereign (equipped with Wings / Flyer or Jump mobility) or a Ruinstorm Harbinger (equipped with Wings / Jump mobility) as the army's Warlord.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="485f-cea5-75b6-752c" name="Effects" hidden="false">
                  <description>• Terrors of the Upper Air: Ruinstorm Sky-Ray Packs and winged Ruinstorm Daemon Beasts (such as Furies or Screamers) may be selected as Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War. Any unit selected as a Compulsory Troops choice in this manner gains the Line Unit Sub-type.
• Swooping Predators: Every model in a Detachment using this Rite of War with the Flyer Unit Type, the Jump Unit Sub-type, or the Sky-Hunter special rule gains the Hit &amp; Run and Fleet (2) special rules (or improves an existing Fleet value by +1).
• Aerial Ambush: The controlling player may add +1 to all Reserves rolls made for units arriving via Deep Strike or Outflank in a Detachment using this Rite of War, and units arriving via Deep Strike may re-roll their scatter distance dice.
• Raking Talons: Models with the Flyer Unit Type or Jump Unit Sub-type in this Detachment add +1 to their Hammer of Wrath and Slashing Dive attack rolls.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="caa2-5f6a-8bce-8498" name="Limitations" hidden="false">
                  <description>• Every unit in a Detachment using this Rite of War must possess the Flyer Unit Type, the Jump Unit Sub-type, the Sky-Hunter special rule, or be joined by a character with one of those rules. Ground-bound units that cannot fly or skim (such as Ruinstorm Daemon Brutes, Cataclysm Brute Packs, Flesh-Reaper Cavalry, and Soul-Forge Engines) may not be included in the Detachment.
• A Detachment using this Rite of War may not select any Fortification choices.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Swarming Horde of the Veil" hidden="false" id="e03d-6e72-93ea-125b">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" field="4974-b321-0d35-6137" value="0">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="and">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="2f3f-adc4-b19f-a5c7" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
                        <condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="5a2e-abe2-3044-3c1c" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
                <modifier type="set" field="4974-b321-0d35-6137" value="0">
                  <conditionGroups>
                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="7031-469a-1aeb-eab0" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
