                    <conditionGroup type="or">
                      <conditions>
                        <condition type="atLeast" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="20ef-cd01-a8da-376e" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
                      </conditions>
                    </conditionGroup>
                  </conditionGroups>
                </modifier>
              </modifiers>
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="0ac6-324b-d15f-632b" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule id="b17e-3684-9ba5-38c7" name="Prerequisites" hidden="false">
                  <description>• A Detachment using this Rite of War must be aligned to the Putrid Corruption Ætheric Dominion, and must include a Ruinstorm Daemon Sovereign or Ruinstorm Harbinger equipped with the Putrid Corruption Ætheric Blessing as the army's Warlord.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="1f92-91b3-f03f-a417" name="Effects" hidden="false">
                  <description>• Garden of Rot: Ruinstorm Daemon Brutes and Ruinstorm Daemon Beasts may be selected as Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War. Any Ruinstorm Lesser Daemon Swarm or Ruinstorm Daemon Brute unit selected as a Compulsory Troops choice gains the Line Unit Sub-type and Heart of the Legion.
• Miasma of Decay: All Ruinstorm Daemon Behemoths, Soul-Forge Engines, and Cataclysm Brute Packs in a Detachment using this Rite of War improve their It Will Not Die roll by +1 (to a maximum of 4+), and enemy units within 6" of any model with the Putrid Corruption Ætheric Blessing suffer a -1 penalty to their Toughness and Initiative Characteristics (to a minimum of 1).
• Virulent Bile: Any Ruinstorm Warp-Spawn Pack or Cataclysm Brute Pack equipped with Corrosive Bile Spray or Bile-Mortar Cannons improves the Poisoned value of those weapons to Poisoned (2+).</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="c277-0afa-6733-e843" name="Limitations" hidden="false">
                  <description>• No unit in a Detachment using this Rite of War may make Run moves in the Shooting phase or Sweeping Advances in the Assault phase.
• A Detachment using this Rite of War may not include any Fast Attack choices (such as Ruinstorm Sky-Ray Packs or Ruinstorm Flesh-Reaper Cavalry).
• Every eligible unit in the Detachment must purchase the Putrid Corruption Ætheric Blessing.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Conflagration of Change (Infernal Tempest)" hidden="false" id="0efd-e6e2-acb8-3d67">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
                  <conditions>
                    <condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="e4fb-66cd-e07d-609b" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
