              </constraints>
              <rules>
                <rule id="22c3-7464-4306-22b4" name="Prerequisites" hidden="false">
                  <description>• A Detachment using this Rite of War must be aligned to the Infernal Tempest Ætheric Dominion, and must include a Ruinstorm Daemon Sovereign or Ruinstorm Harbinger with the Psyker Unit Sub-type and the Infernal Tempest Ætheric Blessing as the army's Warlord.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="b61a-38dd-80d7-ff08" name="Effects" hidden="false">
                  <description>• Riders of the Warp-Storm: Ruinstorm Sky-Ray Packs and Ruinstorm Incinerator Swarms may be selected as Troops choices in a Detachment using this Rite of War. Any unit selected as a Compulsory Troops choice in this manner gains the Line Unit Sub-type.
• Conduits of Etheric Fire: Ruinstorm Incinerator Swarms, Warp-Spawn Packs, Herald Conclaves, and Cataclysm Brute Packs in a Detachment using this Rite of War add +6" to the range of all non-Template ranged weapons and Psychic Weapons, and re-roll failed Soul Blaze rolls at the end of the turn.
• Flickering Mirage: During the first game turn, and during any turn in which a unit arrived via Deep Strike, all friendly units with the Daemon Unit Type in a Detachment using this Rite of War gain the Shrouded (5+) special rule.
• Sudden Manifestation: Add +1 to all Reserves rolls made for units arriving via Deep Strike in a Detachment using this Rite of War.</description>
                </rule>
                <rule id="fdc6-00bb-9287-2c50" name="Limitations" hidden="false">
                  <description>• Every unit in a Detachment using this Rite of War must have the Deep Strike special rule and must be placed into Deep Strike Reserves during deployment (units that cannot deploy via Deep Strike, such as Ruinstorm Soul-Forge Engines, may not be included in the Detachment).
• Every eligible unit in the Detachment must purchase the Infernal Tempest Ætheric Blessing.</description>
                </rule>
              </rules>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
              </costs>
            </selectionEntry>
            <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Carnival of Excess (Rapturous Sensation)" hidden="false" id="195d-8f64-67f1-47ba">
              <modifiers>
                <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
                  <conditions>
